        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.9,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.141,
            0.593,
            0.182
          ],
          "content": "Since, we know the height of the building AB, we will first consider the right $\\Delta   \\mathrm { P A B }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.208,
            0.191,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": "We have"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.293,
            0.195,
            0.442,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "\\tan 3 0 ^ { \\circ } = { \\frac { \\mathrm { A B } } { \\mathrm { A P } } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.268,
            0.14,
            0.287
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.325,
            0.254,
            0.439,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": "{ \\frac { 1 } { \\sqrt { 3 } } } \\; = \\; { \\frac { 1 0 } { \\mathrm { A P } } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.315,
            0.205,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.331,
            0.31,
            0.454,
            0.335
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm { A P } = { \\stackrel { \\cdot } { 1 0 { \\sqrt { 3 } } } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.488,
            0.138,
            0.898,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.652,
                0.317,
                0.74,
                0.337
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 9.7"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.365,
            0.687,
            0.386
          ],
          "content": "i.e., the distance of the building from P is $10\\sqrt{3}\\  m =17.32\\  m .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.398,
            0.632,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": "Next, let us suppose $\\mathrm { D B } = x   \\mathrm { m }$ . Then $\\mathrm{AD} = (10 + x)   \\mathrm{m}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.452,
            0.308,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": "Now, in right   PAD,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.39,
            0.437,
            0.627,
            0.481
          ],
          "content": "\\tan 45^{\\circ} = \\frac{ AD }{ AP } = \\frac{10 \\mp x}{10\\sqrt{3}}",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.511,
            0.205,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.446,
            0.499,
            0.565,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{10 + x}{10\\sqrt{3}}",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.565,
            0.14,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.349,
            0.556,
            0.585,
            0.587
          ],
          "content": "x = 10 \\left( \\sqrt{3} - 1 \\right) = 7.32",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.597,
            0.479,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm { S o } ,$ the length of the flagstaff is 7.32 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.63,
            0.517,
            0.708
          ],
          "content": "**Example 5 :** The shadow of a tower standing on a level ground is found to be 40 m longer when the Sun’s altitude is $3 0 ^ { \\circ }$ than when it is $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ . Find the height of the tower."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.713,
            0.518,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** In Fig. 9.8, AB is the tower and BC is the length of the shadow when the $\\mathrm { S u n } ^ { \\mathrm { { \\textquotesingle } } } \\mathrm { s }$ altitude is $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ , i.e., the angle of elevation of the top of the tower from the tip of the shadow is $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ and DB is the length of the shadow, when the angle of elevation is $3 0 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.531,
            0.599,
            0.902,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.667,
                0.78,
                0.755,
                0.8
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 9.8"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_22.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.861,
            0.902,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": "Now, let AB be h m and BC be x m. According to the question, DB is 40 m longer than BC."
        },
        {
